    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.single_source_shortest_path_length -\n    EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.single_source_shortest_path_length.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.single_source_shortest_path_length()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function\n    .doc-label .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Get the shortest-path distance from one node to every node it can reach.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.single_source_shortest_path_length()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function\n    .doc-label .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Get the shortest-path distance from one node to every node it can reach.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.single_source_shortest_path_length()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function\n  .doc-label .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: >-\n  Get the shortest-path distance from one node to every node it can reach.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nGet the shortest-path distance from one node to every node it can reach.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L61315-L61449){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.single_source_shortest_path_length(\n    source,\n    cutoff=None,\n    attr_name=None,\n    return_dict=False,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Single-source shortest path lengths](../assets/graphs/single-source-shortest-path-length.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"The directed weighted graph with the source A outlined and each node's distance from A in a badge: A 0.0, B 1.0, E 2.0, C and D 3.0, and F 4.0, reached along the accent edges. The table lists the same distances from nearest to farthest.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nRuns one search from `source=` and records how far away every reachable node is: the\nnumber of hops on an unweighted graph, or the lowest total edge weight (Dijkstra's\nalgorithm) on a weighted graph (`Graph(weighted=True)`). Directed graphs are followed in\nedge direction.\n\nDistances from a single point of interest are useful for:\n\n- ego-network analysis (\"everyone within two steps of this person\")\n- service areas and catchments (\"which stations are within 10 minutes\")\n- shading or sizing nodes by how far they are from a focal node\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[source]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Union[int, str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The starting node, as an integer ID or a string label.\n\n<code>[cutoff]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [float | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Only include nodes at distance at most this value. If `None` (default), there is\n    no limit.\n\n<code>[attr_name]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Name of the node attribute to store distances in. If `None` (default), uses\n    `\"single_source_shortest_path_length\"`. Nodes that are not reached get a null value.\n\n<code>[return_dict]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, returns a dictionary instead of self. If `False` (default), stores the\n    distances as a node attribute and returns self for chaining.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Union[dict[int, int | float], Graph]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `return_dict=` is `True`: a dictionary mapping each reachable node ID to its\n    distance (`int` hops on an unweighted graph, `float` on a weighted graph); the\n    source maps to `0`. If `return_dict=` is `False` (default): returns self.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the label does not exist in the graph, or a weighted graph has a negative edge\n    weight.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~single_source_shortest_path`) \n\n:   The paths themselves.\n\n[](`~multi_source_shortest_path_length`) \n\n:   The distance to the nearest of several sources.\n\n[](`~single_target_shortest_path_length`) \n\n:   The distances from every node to a target.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nDistances from one end of a path count up hop by hop:\n\n::: {#5ebe3e19 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\"), (\"D\", \"E\")]\n)\n\ndist = graph.single_source_shortest_path_length(\"A\", return_dict=True)\n{graph.get_label_from_id(n): d for n, d in sorted(dist.items())}\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n{'A': 0, 'B': 1, 'C': 2, 'D': 3, 'E': 4}\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nWithout `return_dict=`, the distances are stored on the nodes; with `cutoff=` the\nnodes beyond it are left null:\n\n::: {#664820e3 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\n(\n    graph\n    .single_source_shortest_path_length(\"C\", cutoff=1, attr_name=\"near_C\")\n    .get_node_df()\n    .select([\"label\", \"near_C\"])\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (5, 2)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>label</th><th>near_C</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>i64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;A&quot;</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;B&quot;</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;C&quot;</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;D&quot;</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;E&quot;</td><td>null</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Minutes from Central\n\n`metro()` is a made-up city's metro network, with each stretch of track weighted by its\ntravel time in minutes. Every station is within 14 minutes of Central, and the farthest\nare the Airport, Garden and Hillcrest:\n\n::: {#050beeee .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro = ec.metro().single_source_shortest_path_length(\n    \"Central\", attr_name=\"minutes\"\n)\n\nmetro.plot(\n    layout=\"pos\", color_by=\"minutes\", color_scale=\"sequential\",\n    label_by=\"label\",\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-4eae359b:#74a3dc;--ect-8eff6c8a:#406ba2;--ect-e76ae989:#5986be;--ect-66b03f8b:#618fc7;--ect-6425850a:#0d366b;--ect-850c075a:#376299;--ect-975840b8:#86b6ef;--ect-f8094ac6:#79a8e1;--ect-472663e1:#6d9bd3;--ect-6826a